    "title": "Who Else Wants to Know?",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23540849",
    "publication_date": "2026-10-21",
    "description": "<p><span>AI could help people discover questions they hadn&rsquo;t imagined, connect them with unfamiliar sources and </span><span>measurement capabilities, and bring buyers together to fund new observations. This speculative essay </span><span>explores that possibility through freight, weather and urban infrastructure examples. It considers how </span><span>shared purchases can support lasting observation capability while buyers remain unknown to one another, </span><span>and how funding choices shape which questions get investigated.</span></p>",
